Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.31.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.31.0 (archive 33): (1) P7-geom crash regression + self-shrinking-to-minimum window both traced to 0.30 applying transform/anchorPoint directly to the content area, which lives on the autoresizing/presenter layout chain - setting frame on a view with non-identity transform is undefined behavior (Stheno can scale its own standalone container because it is not on the FBScene presentation chain); the live zoom now scales a standalone snapshot preview view created at drag start (zero layout chain, anchor surgery safe, userInteractionEnabled=NO), removed on End/Cancel/rollback; the content area itself is never transformed again; (2) windowLevel auto-raise verified working on device (SBStatusBarWindow level=999 -> floating window 1099). 0.30.0 (archive 32): (1) Stheno-style live zoom replicated from Stheno.dylib evidence (_dragScale/baseScaleLast/finalScale/containerScale): during the resize drag the content area is transform-scaled in real time (anchor pinned at the opposite corner, exactly Stheno finalCardCorner), zero scene writes so the presenter stays alive - the frozen-content-until-release behavior is gone; transform + anchor are reset on End/Cancel/misfire-rollback before the final scene.frame sync; (2) freeze-after-shrinking-to-minimum fixed with a heal watcher: when the guard stops because scene.isValid stays NO for 3 beats, a 0.5s x30 observer waits for the scene to come back and then restarts the guard and re-syncs geometry automatically (previously the hosting stayed dead until the user re-hosted manually); (3) windowLevel auto-raise now actually finds a target: MFClassSharedInstance(UIStatusBarWindow) returned nil on device (log: level=-1), so the probe now enumerates UIApplication.windows preferring a class containing StatusBar and falls back to the highest windowLevel in process, then raises the floating window to that + 100 (Stheno UIStatusBarWindowHook/setWindowLevel: style). 0.29.0 (archive 31): (1) ROOT CAUSE of dead touches after rapid resizes found - the drag-time scene.frame writes themselves invalidate the presenter (log: presenter isActive=0 isHosting=0 isInvalidated=1 during resize, scene.isValid stays NO for 3+ beats, i.e. a genuine >=600ms teardown that no guard rule can ride out); all scene.settings writes during the drag are now removed - the window frame moves locally, and scene geometry is synced exactly once on release plus one confirmation sync 800 ms later (after the async app relayout lands), which also targets the cropped/zoomed look caused by the presentation view lagging behind the app relayout; (2) the windowLevel auto-raise never ran because the default config ships windowLevel=@1010 which counted as explicitly configured - 1010 is now treated as unset so the floating window really raises to UIStatusBarWindow.windowLevel + 100 for touch routing above foreground apps. 0.28.0 (archive 30): (1) touch/click death inside the panel after a few rapid resizes fixed at the root: FBScene.isValid flips NO for a single beat during layer-drop windows and the old guard killed itself on the first NO, leaving nobody to pull the scene back to contentState=2 (visible but non-interactive); isValid must now stay NO for 3 consecutive beats before the guard stops, transient NO beats are just skipped; (2) dead gestures while an app is foreground: 0.27 proved the status-bar window shares the main scene, so the fix moved to window arbitration - when no explicit windowLevel is configured the floating window now auto-raises to UIStatusBarWindow.windowLevel + 100 (the status bar window keeps touch routing over apps, Dynamic Island taps prove it); (3) the visually non-proportional resize (math was exact 0.535 AR all along) is the stretch of the presentationView while win.frame is ahead of scene.frame - the drag-time sync throttle is tightened 250ms -> 120ms to shrink the gap. 0.27.0 (archive 29): (1) not-running apps launch suspended:YES - Stheno's exact way - so nothing goes fullscreen first and the desktop stays visible behind the floating window (no more black background / manual back-to-home); (2) resize keeps showing LIVE content: during the gesture the snapshot pad is neither raised to the top nor left covering (it is lowered immediately), because the frequent layer drops during a drag made the frozen snapshot mask the real render; (3) corner radius 16 -> 24; (4) default floating window size is now Stheno-style tall card 0.55 x 0.72 of the screen, configurable via new defaultWidthScale / defaultHeightScale keys (cfgVersion 21); (5) the floating window now prefers the always-active UIStatusBarWindow scene (guessing the inactive-main-scene touch routing as the cause of dead gestures while an app is foreground; falls back to the main scene). 0.26.0: archive 28 fixes - (1) close/reload buttons were untouchable because their container had userInteractionEnabled=NO which kills the whole subtree's touches (container now left default); (2) hosted app corners are clipped with a 16 pt radius on the content area itself (window corner no longer covers the content since the trim ring was added); (3) the frozen-snapshot look during resize is gone: scene.frame is now throttled-synced (250 ms) while dragging so live content follows the finger; (4) launching a not-running app now uses UIApplication's private launchApplicationWithIdentifier:suspended:NO (the exact channel FrontBoardAppLauncher and Stheno use - FBSOpenApplicationService proved unusable: no +sharedInstance and no openApplication selector on instances). 0.25.0 reproduces Stheno's out-of-frame gesture model 1:1 (reverse-engineered from Stheno.dylib: cardTrim / EdgeBarControlView / PanGestureSubType / finalCardCorner): the window is now the content area plus an 18 pt invisible trim ring on all four sides; edges drag the window, corners resize it proportionally with the opposite corner pinned (incremental accumulation kept - the anchor is only used for origin derivation), a double tap anywhere on the trim toggles the app picker, and the hosted app receives every touch inside the content area like before. The old inner strips and the corner grip are gone; the reload/close buttons float small and translucent at the content's top-right. Also fixes archive 27: FBSOpenApplicationService has no +sharedInstance (unrecognized selector) - it is now created via alloc/init, so tapping a not-running app really launches it and auto-hosts 2 s later. No new config keys; cfgVersion stays 20.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
